NAMING / CASE-COLLISION NOTE  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  This prompt's surface is `AiUsageCard` (web features/system/components/status/AiUsageCard.tsx). A DIFFERENT,
  already-shipped surface 0203 `AIUsageCard` (web features/settings/components/AIUsageCard.tsx) occupies
  feature-views/AIUsageCard.*. The two are distinct surfaces (settings "Usage today" 3-cell card vs this operator
  bands/details/top-lists card) but their file stems differ only by the case of one letter ("Ai" vs "AI"). The
  repo's git index is case-sensitive and is intended to hold BOTH; the LOCAL macOS volume is case-INSENSITIVE
  (core.ignorecase=true, verified), so the two stems cannot both materialise on disk at once. Writing AiUsageCard.*
  directly would overwrite 0203's AIUsageCard.* bytes. To ship 0237 correctly WITHOUT touching 0203 the new files
  were committed via git plumbing (git hash-object -w + git write-tree from a temp index seeded with `read-tree
  HEAD`), so the commit tree contains BOTH surfaces as distinct blobs. 0203's 7 AIUsageCard.* blob SHAs were
  snapshotted before and re-verified byte-identical after (88a7247 / 8551 / ed55 / 8e67 / 5e7d / bbf6 / 792f —
  unchanged). On this case-insensitive checkout `git status` will report the new AiUsageCard.* as "deleted in
  worktree" (only AIUsageCard.* can sit on disk) — this is an expected checkout artifact of two case-variant
  paths, NOT corruption; a case-sensitive CI checkout materialises both.

